---
description: WebXXL source-grounded continuity and no-drift requirements
alwaysApply: true
---

Read root `AGENTS.md`, `docs/PROJECT_MEMORY.md`, `docs/SESSION_HANDOFF.md`, and `docs/platform/docs/00-SESSION-START.md` before starting WebXXL coding. Evidence order: GitHub, then Vercel (SHA only), then repo docs, then ChatGPT/v0 coordination — never invent merge/deploy/migration state. Keep the six-field canonical checkpoint identical in `PROJECT_MEMORY.md` and `SESSION_HANDOFF.md`. An open PR is not merged. Read Master TAD and relevant domain spec before changing architecture. Use current origin/main and real files, never conversation recollection as release proof. Cursor owns nonvisual code/docs/CI/Git; v0.app alone owns UI/UX; avoid overlapping changes. No production migration/flags/sends/charges/schedules/DNS without separate owner authorization. Keep every PR bounded, source-tested and unmerged for owner review; update impacted continuity docs and exact session handoff. Distinguish merged/deployed/migrated/activated/verified. Check legacy ADR-001..017 and `docs/adr/INDEX.md` before major architectural or vendor changes. New ADR-018+ drafts start PROPOSED and need explicit owner evidence plus canonical decision-log entry before APPROVED. The stale-status advisory warns when a MERGED batch or PR recorded in `docs/PROJECT_MEMORY.md` is still described as open. It does not compare documentation to the current commit SHA. `WEBXXL HANDOFF` is the final session record: verified main SHA, branch, PR, head SHA, merge status, last completed batch, changes, validations, deployment, migration, activation, providers, decisions, blockers, deferrals, next assignment, and repository sync status. Update the affected living-blueprint files in the working PR before reporting completion. `PENDING REPOSITORY SYNC` marks a material ChatGPT or v0.app fact that is not yet committed; name the fact, target file, responsible platform, and next action, and clear it only after the commit and the PR or merge are recorded. An open PR is not merged. v0.app UI handoffs list edited paths and verification evidence; Cursor reconciles them. ChatGPT does not claim a session end wrote the repository.
